WEBVTT

00:00:04.972 --> 00:00:07.241
- [thunder rumbles]
- [rain falling]

00:00:10.478 --> 00:00:11.879
[thunder crashes]

00:00:17.451 --> 00:00:20.054
[phone rings]

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.791
[Angel over phone]
Hermano, <i>I'm outside.</i>

00:00:23.891 --> 00:00:26.594
<i>I got an address
on the New York Ripper.</i>

00:00:26.694 --> 00:00:28.696
♪ exciting music ♪

00:00:50.218 --> 00:00:51.252
Cubano.

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:53.287
Nice. What do we know?

00:00:53.387 --> 00:00:56.390
The Ripper's been tracked
to a building in Five Points.

00:00:56.524 --> 00:00:59.227
Nobody fits the Code
more than the Ripper.

00:00:59.327 --> 00:01:02.163
<i>- Tan cierto, mi amigo.</i>
- ["The Heat Is On" playing]

00:01:03.464 --> 00:01:05.566
<i>♪ The heat is on ♪</i>

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.636
<i>♪ On the street ♪</i>

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.639
<i>♪ Inside your head ♪</i>

00:01:13.407 --> 00:01:14.942
<i>♪ On every beat ♪</i>

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.745
- <i>♪ And the beat's so loud... ♪</i>
- [mechanical whirring]

00:01:17.845 --> 00:01:19.880
[Angel]
"Hell awaits"?

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.914
You think?

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:25.153
<i>♪ The pressure's high ♪</i>

00:01:25.253 --> 00:01:27.921
<i>♪ Just to stay alive ♪</i>

00:01:28.055 --> 00:01:31.292
<i>♪ 'Cause the heat is on ♪</i>

00:01:35.796 --> 00:01:37.531
<i>♪ Caught up in the action ♪</i>

00:01:37.631 --> 00:01:39.466
<i>♪ I've been looking out
for you ♪</i>

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.835
<i>♪ The heat is on ♪</i>

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:45.573
<i>♪ The heat is on... ♪</i>

00:01:45.673 --> 00:01:47.441
So eager to die.

00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:48.842
[grunting]

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.445
<i>♪ Oh, it's on the street ♪</i>

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.315
<i>♪ The heat is ♪</i>

00:01:54.415 --> 00:01:56.116
<i>♪ On ♪</i>

00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:58.486
♪ atmospheric music ♪

00:02:05.426 --> 00:02:07.628
[muffled grunting]

00:02:15.636 --> 00:02:17.004
All right, brother.

00:02:17.771 --> 00:02:19.707
Make the world a better place.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.747
Hell awaits.

00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:32.085
Fuck you, Dexter Morgan.

00:02:33.587 --> 00:02:34.854
[screams]

00:02:34.855 --> 00:02:36.257
[phone chimes]

00:02:42.363 --> 00:02:44.163
[inhales deeply]

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.866
[exhales]

00:02:50.137 --> 00:02:52.373
[Harry]
<i>You miss him.</i>

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.842
Angel's death wasn't your fault.

00:02:54.942 --> 00:02:57.511
He turned on me.
I was the one who freed him.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.984
But you know Angel
couldn't accept who you are,

00:03:04.084 --> 00:03:05.185
what you are.

00:03:05.319 --> 00:03:06.887
[scoffs]

00:03:07.721 --> 00:03:09.923
I wish he could have.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.227
[sighs]

00:03:15.429 --> 00:03:17.698
["Needles, CA" by SUSS playing]

00:03:27.641 --> 00:03:28.942
[groans]

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.744
[bottle clatters]

00:03:32.913 --> 00:03:34.047
- [phone chimes]
- Yo.

00:03:34.181 --> 00:03:36.450
Dude, you got
any mints up there?

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:41.221
Nope. Sorry.

00:03:41.322 --> 00:03:43.089
<i>Dude.</i>

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.025
All right, well, can you
change the music, at least?

00:03:45.125 --> 00:03:48.061
Uh, satellite radio
hyperpop station.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:52.065
<i>♪ Dying culture pop,
the famous moldy party hop ♪</i>

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.434
<i>♪ The point of view,
the bleeding heart ♪</i>

00:03:54.435 --> 00:03:55.569
<i>♪ The easily digested hurt ♪</i>

00:03:56.404 --> 00:03:58.706
<i>♪ The psychotronic talking box,
the mainstream antidepressant ♪</i>

00:03:59.773 --> 00:04:01.108
<i>♪ The silly putty tinker toy ♪</i>

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.643
<i>♪ The mirror ball
reflects below ♪</i>

00:04:05.346 --> 00:04:07.247
[music stops]

00:04:07.381 --> 00:04:09.617
And here you are.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.452
This isn't my fucking drop-off.

00:04:17.291 --> 00:04:19.792
[Dexter] I must've gotten the
three and the eight mixed up.

00:04:19.793 --> 00:04:21.194
It's only a couple of blocks.
I can--

00:04:21.295 --> 00:04:22.596
I'll walk it.

00:04:24.565 --> 00:04:27.335
I'm about to close
an $80 million dollar deal,

00:04:27.435 --> 00:04:29.470
and you can't even take someone
to the right address?

00:04:29.603 --> 00:04:32.906
[scoffs]
What a life you live, boomer.

00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:36.109
[Dexter]
<i>Boomer?</i>

00:04:36.877 --> 00:04:38.445
Generation X, dipshit.

00:04:38.446 --> 00:04:41.615
<i>People like that
make me question the Code.</i>

00:04:43.517 --> 00:04:45.419
<i>Since the day Prater's vault</i>

00:04:45.519 --> 00:04:47.955
<i>was discovered by the NYPD,</i>

00:04:48.055 --> 00:04:51.525
<i>the five living serial killers
from Prater's boogeyman club</i>

00:04:51.625 --> 00:04:53.761
<i>went into hiding.</i>

00:04:54.495 --> 00:04:55.963
<i>And while the police
thought Prater</i>

00:04:56.063 --> 00:04:58.198
<i>disappeared to some private island...</i>

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:03.170
<i>...I managed to find
two of the killers.</i>

00:05:04.438 --> 00:05:05.506
♪ "Masterpiece Theatre Theme"
by Eric Hammerstein playing ♪

00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:06.807
<i>The Midnight Mangler</i>

00:05:06.907 --> 00:05:08.141
<i>was the first.</i>

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:09.743
<i>This monster
captured his victims,</i>

00:05:09.843 --> 00:05:11.512
<i>held them for two weeks,</i>

00:05:11.612 --> 00:05:13.547
<i>breaking their bones one by one</i>

00:05:13.647 --> 00:05:15.648
<i>before finally killing them
at midnight.</i>

00:05:15.649 --> 00:05:17.718
- ♪ intense music
<i>- Thirty-two victims</i>

00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:19.820
<i>in his eight-year
reign of terror.</i>

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.889
<i>His cruelty knew no end,</i>

00:05:21.989 --> 00:05:25.493
<i>until that night in Seattle
when he met me.</i>

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:31.264
Who's this? What is this?

00:05:31.365 --> 00:05:32.900
Aah!

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.167
No, no.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:37.705
No, you can't do this. No.

00:05:37.805 --> 00:05:39.707
Oh, I think I can.

00:05:39.807 --> 00:05:41.509
No, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no...

00:05:41.609 --> 00:05:42.676
No!

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.044
[ragged exhale]

00:05:45.045 --> 00:05:48.115
[Dexter] <i>If I hadn't
captured and killed him...</i>

00:05:48.215 --> 00:05:49.517
<i>...there could have been</i>

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:52.686
<i>another 32 innocent victims
murdered.</i>

00:05:54.788 --> 00:05:57.925
<i>The Yonkers Slayer
was a self-proclaimed satanist</i>

00:05:58.025 --> 00:06:01.228
<i>who ritually murdered
more than 20 people.</i>

00:06:02.029 --> 00:06:03.730
<i>Needless to say, he claimed...</i>

00:06:03.731 --> 00:06:06.099
The devil made me do it.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.601
Don't.

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.236
It must be nice

00:06:09.336 --> 00:06:12.473
to blame your actions
on someone other than yourself.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:22.082
<i>By slaying this Slayer,
I figure I've saved</i>

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:24.117
<i>at least another 20 people.</i>

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:27.087
Welcome to hell, Mr. Slayer.

00:06:29.557 --> 00:06:31.525
<i>Unfortunately for me,</i>

00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:33.661
<i>gentrification is turning this building</i>

00:06:33.761 --> 00:06:36.063
<i>into a Whole Foods.</i>

00:06:36.163 --> 00:06:38.966
<i>Goodbye, surefire body disposal.</i>

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.035
<i>And that makes 13,</i>

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:44.472
<i>an unlucky number...</i>

00:06:45.272 --> 00:06:47.074
<i>...for everyone but me.</i>

00:06:47.174 --> 00:06:48.741
♪ somber music ♪

00:06:48.742 --> 00:06:51.110
<i>And yet nobody even knows.</i>

00:06:51.111 --> 00:06:53.080
[phone chimes]

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:57.050
<i>This is hardly the life
I imagined I'd have in my 50s.</i>

00:06:57.150 --> 00:07:00.621
You never even imagined you'd
still be alive in your 50s.

00:07:00.721 --> 00:07:04.124
Yeah, it's not like serial
killers get retirement plans.

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:06.560
All the good I've done
in the world,

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.029
and still living
a two-star life.

00:07:09.129 --> 00:07:11.331
You've always been
five stars to me, kiddo.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.766
[Dexter]
<i>Great.</i>

00:07:12.866 --> 00:07:15.202
<i>My dead dad gives me five stars.</i>

00:07:24.044 --> 00:07:26.313
♪ quirky music ♪

00:07:51.238 --> 00:07:52.873
♪

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:23.904
♪

00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:54.034
♪

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.882
♪ upbeat music ♪

00:09:10.851 --> 00:09:12.519
[Harrison] So, my six months

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.155
at the police academy
are finally over.

00:09:15.255 --> 00:09:16.657
Congratulations.

00:09:16.757 --> 00:09:18.592
Definitely not gonna miss
the gun range.

00:09:18.692 --> 00:09:19.827
Constant shooting,

00:09:19.927 --> 00:09:21.561
coming home smelling like
fucking cordite.

00:09:21.662 --> 00:09:23.463
Can't... [scoffs]
can't wash that shit off.

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:25.733
I never liked guns, either.

00:09:25.866 --> 00:09:27.367
So loud.

00:09:27.467 --> 00:09:28.736
Imprecise.

00:09:28.836 --> 00:09:31.404
And no more fucking tests.

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:34.440
Just, l-like, real work.

00:09:34.441 --> 00:09:36.275
I-I think I'm actually
looking forward

00:09:36.276 --> 00:09:37.611
to the day-to-day grind
of the street.

00:09:37.745 --> 00:09:40.080
Plus, my salary
practically doubles.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.514
Nice.

00:09:43.116 --> 00:09:45.485
You're-you're coming to my
gun and shield ceremony, right?

00:09:45.585 --> 00:09:46.754
Wouldn't miss it.

00:09:48.488 --> 00:09:51.625
And, hey, uh, no more living
with five knuckleheads

00:09:51.725 --> 00:09:52.826
in a tiny apartment.

00:09:52.926 --> 00:09:54.962
I've already got
a new place lined up.

00:09:56.129 --> 00:09:57.263
Good for you.

00:09:57.264 --> 00:09:59.966
Thing is, um...

00:09:59.967 --> 00:10:02.769
you know, with a-with a
y-yearlong lease

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:05.305
and, uh, security deposit...

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:07.340
I'm happy to cosign your lease,

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.843
- pay your up-front costs.
- You sure?

00:10:09.943 --> 00:10:11.544
Yeah, I sold
the Iron Lake property

00:10:11.645 --> 00:10:14.781
for a good price,
and still have that cash

00:10:14.782 --> 00:10:17.985
from our dearly departed friend,
so it's not a problem.

00:10:18.118 --> 00:10:19.653
Thanks, Dad.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:24.057
Also, uh, a-about
our phone plan, um...

00:10:24.157 --> 00:10:27.627
Now that I'm 21,
can I-can I stay on yours?

00:10:27.728 --> 00:10:29.897
Yeah, I got you covered.
And, um...

00:10:29.997 --> 00:10:31.799
you know, with you
about to start working

00:10:31.899 --> 00:10:33.600
crazy hours in crazy places,

00:10:33.701 --> 00:10:36.336
it might not be a bad idea
if we share locations.

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:39.638
[scoffs] You're the one with
crazy hours in crazy places,

00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:42.309
- so yeah.
- Yeah.

00:10:47.748 --> 00:10:49.649
♪ gentle music ♪

00:10:49.783 --> 00:10:50.784
What?

00:10:50.884 --> 00:10:53.352
When you first came to New York,

00:10:53.353 --> 00:10:55.622
you were homeless, lost.

00:10:55.723 --> 00:10:58.859
Now you got a career,
a path, a home.

00:11:00.427 --> 00:11:01.828
I'm proud of you.

00:11:01.829 --> 00:11:03.430
Thanks.

00:11:06.834 --> 00:11:08.769
Where were you
when you were my age?

00:11:08.869 --> 00:11:10.570
Hmm.

00:11:11.772 --> 00:11:14.074
I was already working
Miami Metro Homicide,

00:11:14.174 --> 00:11:17.277
and my other career
was off to a good start.

00:11:19.179 --> 00:11:21.882
I knew what I wanted to do,
and I was doing it.

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.017
It's a great feeling,

00:11:25.018 --> 00:11:26.685
when your plans
start to take shape

00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:29.689
and you got your whole life
ahead of you.

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:34.194
You gonna eat that?

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.066
Oh, d-did you mean that one?

00:11:39.166 --> 00:11:42.035
You're a cop now.
That's called theft.

00:11:42.135 --> 00:11:44.037
And I got to run.
[chuckles]

00:11:44.137 --> 00:11:45.372
You want a ride?

00:11:45.472 --> 00:11:46.807
Mm, no offense,
but the subway's,

00:11:46.907 --> 00:11:48.575
like, way quicker than a UrCar.

00:11:48.708 --> 00:11:49.708
Same time next week?

00:11:49.709 --> 00:11:51.144
I don't really know, actually.

00:11:51.244 --> 00:11:53.046
I'm not... I'm not
my own boss anymore.

00:11:53.146 --> 00:11:55.882
Okay.
Well, I am my own boss,

00:11:55.883 --> 00:11:58.618
so I can make whatever time
works for you.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.454
Thanks, Dad.

00:12:05.525 --> 00:12:07.094
[Harry]
Your own boss?

00:12:07.194 --> 00:12:09.362
[laughs softly] More like
you've got a dozen bosses a day

00:12:09.462 --> 00:12:12.132
who are constantly judging you
on a rideshare app.

00:12:12.232 --> 00:12:13.733
Doesn't matter.

00:12:13.834 --> 00:12:16.236
I got a more important job:

00:12:16.336 --> 00:12:18.171
being Harrison's dad.

00:12:19.239 --> 00:12:20.573
He still needs me.

00:12:20.707 --> 00:12:22.675
And you need him.

00:12:25.645 --> 00:12:27.746
[distorted voice]
<i>Sammy, Sammy, Sammy.</i>

00:12:27.747 --> 00:12:30.818
<i>It's your old friend
the New York Ripper calling</i>

00:12:30.918 --> 00:12:34.955
<i>to remind you about your
sweet little angel, Rachel.</i>

00:12:35.055 --> 00:12:36.622
<i>But how could you forget,</i>

00:12:36.623 --> 00:12:38.291
<i>since you're the one
who found her,</i>

00:12:38.391 --> 00:12:41.428
<i>after I nearly
ripped her in two?</i>

00:12:41.561 --> 00:12:44.164
<i>All of her blood and organs
on display</i>

00:12:44.264 --> 00:12:46.566
<i>just for you.</i>

00:12:46.666 --> 00:12:49.101
<i>Making a mess
of your beige carpet.</i>

00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:51.071
<i>You know, I just had a thought.</i>

00:12:51.171 --> 00:12:53.773
<i>If Rachel was still
on this side of the grass,</i>

00:12:53.907 --> 00:12:56.608
<i>you'd probably be a grandpa
by now, huh?</i>

00:12:56.609 --> 00:13:00.480
<i>Well, you win some,
you lose some, I guess.</i>

00:13:00.613 --> 00:13:02.614
<i>Talk soon, Sammy.</i>

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:04.517
<i>I'll call again.</i>

00:13:04.617 --> 00:13:06.653
<i>Buh-bye.</i>

00:13:07.487 --> 00:13:09.322
The call was made
to Sam McCormick,

00:13:09.422 --> 00:13:11.959
father of 15-year-old
victim Rachel,

00:13:12.059 --> 00:13:13.961
at 4:07 a.m. last Wednesday.

00:13:14.061 --> 00:13:15.695
We pinged the call
from a cell phone tower

00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:17.865
1.3 miles from Don Framt's home.

00:13:17.965 --> 00:13:20.500
A hundred and fifty thousand
people live in Williamsburg,

00:13:20.633 --> 00:13:22.936
not to mention all the people
walking or driving through.

00:13:23.036 --> 00:13:25.472
Popular spot.

00:13:25.572 --> 00:13:28.174
Do you deny that it is
your voice on the recording?

00:13:28.175 --> 00:13:29.476
Of course he denies it.

00:13:29.609 --> 00:13:32.145
Where were you at 4:07 a.m.
last Wednesday?

00:13:32.245 --> 00:13:33.881
Out dancing.

00:13:37.084 --> 00:13:39.786
You should
join me sometime, sugar,

00:13:39.887 --> 00:13:44.023
because you sure got
one hell of a dancer's body.

00:13:44.024 --> 00:13:45.525
Ha!

00:13:45.658 --> 00:13:47.027
[chuckles]

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:48.861
Is that the official alibi
you want on the record?

00:13:48.862 --> 00:13:51.932
Mr. Framt was asleep in bed,
like everyone else.

00:13:52.032 --> 00:13:54.167
Now, let me make myself
clear as crystal.

00:13:54.267 --> 00:13:57.204
This is the last time
you drag my client across town.

00:13:57.337 --> 00:14:00.373
- This is full-blown harassment.
- [door opens]

00:14:00.473 --> 00:14:02.609
Mr. Framt, you're free to go.

00:14:02.709 --> 00:14:05.045
I apologize

00:14:05.178 --> 00:14:06.646
for the inconvenience.

00:14:06.746 --> 00:14:10.550
In case you want
to test my DNA...

00:14:13.286 --> 00:14:14.721
...again.

00:14:18.325 --> 00:14:21.528
♪ ominous music ♪

00:14:24.364 --> 00:14:26.466
Get that hound dog of yours

00:14:26.566 --> 00:14:29.269
off my tail.

00:14:38.045 --> 00:14:40.547
How many times have you two

00:14:40.647 --> 00:14:43.716
unsuccessfully
interrogated Framt?

00:14:43.816 --> 00:14:46.586
- Somewhere around--
- Nine times, Captain.

00:14:46.686 --> 00:14:50.023
Not "somewhere around."
Exactly nine times.

00:14:50.123 --> 00:14:51.691
But he will eventually
make a mistake.

00:14:51.791 --> 00:14:54.393
He will eventually give us
something we can use.

00:14:54.394 --> 00:14:56.196
There's no "eventually" here.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.631
[sighs]

00:14:59.666 --> 00:15:01.434
We all know Framt's our guy.

00:15:01.534 --> 00:15:04.071
But you got no hard evidence,
no case.

00:15:04.204 --> 00:15:06.273
Which means, if we were
to take him to court today,

00:15:06.406 --> 00:15:08.008
we would lose...

00:15:09.009 --> 00:15:11.544
...and he can never be tried
for those crimes again.

00:15:11.644 --> 00:15:13.413
We found this file inside

00:15:13.513 --> 00:15:15.581
Leon Prater's
serial killer vault,

00:15:15.582 --> 00:15:17.784
directly beneath the very weapon

00:15:17.917 --> 00:15:19.586
the New York Ripper
used to eviscerate

00:15:19.686 --> 00:15:21.288
and murder his victims.

00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:22.889
Do you know the odds that,
in a room containing

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:25.292
over 100 confirmed
serial killer accoutrement--

00:15:25.392 --> 00:15:27.494
John Wayne Gacy's
Pogo the Clown suit...

00:15:28.428 --> 00:15:30.130
...Mia LaPierre's trophies...

00:15:31.564 --> 00:15:33.466
...the Dark Passenger's
bloodstained driver's license,

00:15:33.566 --> 00:15:35.702
<i>matched to the DNA
of his first victim--</i>

00:15:35.802 --> 00:15:37.004
that the one and only
piece of evidence

00:15:37.104 --> 00:15:38.804
that happens to be incorrect

00:15:38.805 --> 00:15:42.242
would be this file naming Don
Framt as the New York Ripper?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:45.212
Less than one percent.

00:15:45.312 --> 00:15:48.715
0.83%, in fact.

00:15:49.582 --> 00:15:51.084
She had me run the numbers.

00:15:51.184 --> 00:15:52.952
And... yet,

00:15:53.053 --> 00:15:55.122
a file found in a fucked-up room

00:15:55.222 --> 00:15:58.191
isn't enough to convince
a jury of his peers.

00:15:58.291 --> 00:16:00.127
We get one shot...

00:16:01.094 --> 00:16:03.830
...at nailing
this piece of shit.

00:16:05.098 --> 00:16:07.600
So, until we have definitive,

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.570
non-circumstantial proof,

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:12.339
lay off Framt.

00:16:13.173 --> 00:16:15.175
[door closes]

00:16:15.275 --> 00:16:16.675
I have been working this case

00:16:16.676 --> 00:16:19.879
for 23 years.

00:16:19.979 --> 00:16:22.182
I want to solve it before I die.

00:16:22.282 --> 00:16:25.085
And more importantly, I want
to solve it before he dies.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.655
Hey.

00:16:30.123 --> 00:16:33.126
We're not gonna give up
until the Ripper's behind bars.

00:16:33.993 --> 00:16:35.928
I promise.

00:16:41.634 --> 00:16:43.036
[car alarm chirps]

00:16:46.773 --> 00:16:48.207
[Dexter]
<i>After a long day</i>

00:16:48.208 --> 00:16:50.842
<i>of 28 yammering people
in my back seat,</i>

00:16:50.843 --> 00:16:52.945
<i>including that two-star asshole,</i>

00:16:53.046 --> 00:16:54.914
<i>all I crave is silence.</i>

00:16:55.014 --> 00:16:56.715
