No reason for the owner's
grandson to have any memory

00:41:03.495 --> 00:41:04.896
of what's in there.

00:41:05.664 --> 00:41:07.999
It should be ugly enough
for the cops.

00:41:09.200 --> 00:41:10.702
Good on you, son.

00:41:10.802 --> 00:41:12.203
Protecting that boy.

00:41:12.303 --> 00:41:15.040
Sometimes boys need protecting.

00:41:18.510 --> 00:41:20.746
♪ somber music ♪

00:41:25.016 --> 00:41:26.685
[announcer] <i>After a rain delay
of over half an hour,</i>

00:41:26.785 --> 00:41:29.053
<i>the umpires have decided
to postpone tonight's game</i>

00:41:29.054 --> 00:41:31.389
<i>and make tomorrow
a twi-night doubleheader.</i>

00:41:31.489 --> 00:41:33.692
♪ tense music ♪

00:41:52.210 --> 00:41:54.412
[indistinct chatter]

00:42:14.933 --> 00:42:16.935
- Nobody cares.
- What?

00:42:17.035 --> 00:42:18.904
[silenced gunshot]

00:42:27.545 --> 00:42:29.080
["Yankee and the Brave (ep. 4)"
by Run the Jewels playing]

00:42:29.180 --> 00:42:31.082
- Incoming.
- <i>♪ Old Natty, hair nappy ♪</i>

00:42:31.182 --> 00:42:33.284
<i>♪ Matty as a Black granddaddy,
all fact... ♪</i>

00:42:33.418 --> 00:42:35.253
Mind if I hit on your friend?

00:42:36.688 --> 00:42:38.489
[clears throat]

00:42:39.257 --> 00:42:40.892
You can give it your best shot.

00:42:40.992 --> 00:42:42.928
<i>♪ Sauna all summer
and I put that on Osama ♪</i>

00:42:43.061 --> 00:42:44.129
<i>♪ And my... ♪</i>

00:42:44.262 --> 00:42:45.496
I got nothing.

00:42:46.331 --> 00:42:47.933
Never been good
at the art of the line.

00:42:48.066 --> 00:42:49.635
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

00:42:49.768 --> 00:42:51.469
Come on. I'm sure
you hear plenty of 'em.

00:42:51.569 --> 00:42:53.238
Never any good ones.

00:42:54.005 --> 00:42:57.575
Which is why you not trying to
come up with one was refreshing.

00:42:58.376 --> 00:43:01.146
Most cops think
they're so goddamn smooth.

00:43:01.980 --> 00:43:03.815
And you don't like smooth?

00:43:04.983 --> 00:43:07.653
<i>♪ Go-go-go-go, go-go-go-go ♪</i>

00:43:07.753 --> 00:43:10.789
<i>♪ Go-go-go, go-go,
what we gonna do? ♪</i>

00:43:10.889 --> 00:43:13.124
<i>♪ Till time die,
I'm galactically fly ♪</i>

00:43:13.224 --> 00:43:16.160
<i>♪ The moon is moving the maniacs
in the city to crime... ♪</i>

00:43:16.161 --> 00:43:18.129
["An Ocean in Between the Waves"
by The War on Drugs playing]

00:43:18.263 --> 00:43:21.165
<i>♪ Feel the way that the wild
wind blows through the room ♪</i>

00:43:21.166 --> 00:43:22.633
<i>♪ Like a nail... ♪</i>

00:43:22.634 --> 00:43:24.636
- [grunts]
- [Angel] <i>Killing Rapunzel</i>

00:43:24.736 --> 00:43:26.304
<i>is not gonna change anything.</i>

00:43:26.404 --> 00:43:28.073
You're no hero.

00:43:28.173 --> 00:43:30.075
You're not a good guy.

00:43:32.343 --> 00:43:34.345
And how the fuck
is anyone supposed to know

00:43:34.479 --> 00:43:36.181
you took Rapunzel out?

00:43:38.416 --> 00:43:39.985
[hissing]

00:43:40.118 --> 00:43:41.586
Fuck!

00:43:41.687 --> 00:43:43.655
- [breathes heavily]
- <i>♪ Than just a fool? ♪</i>

00:43:43.789 --> 00:43:45.356
[inhales sharply]

00:43:46.992 --> 00:43:50.028
<i>♪ It always gets so hard
to see ♪</i>

00:43:50.128 --> 00:43:52.430
[sniffing]

00:43:52.530 --> 00:43:54.532
Ah.

00:44:04.009 --> 00:44:05.744
Thank you for the update.

00:44:06.845 --> 00:44:08.579
[helicopter flying overhead]

00:44:08.680 --> 00:44:10.048
[Oliva]
Like we thought.

00:44:10.882 --> 00:44:13.351
Rain washed away
any hard evidence.

00:44:14.452 --> 00:44:17.322
CSIs are luminoling,
see what they can find.

00:44:17.422 --> 00:44:18.757
Did you learn anything useful

00:44:18.857 --> 00:44:20.358
- from the security footage?
- [groans]

00:44:20.458 --> 00:44:22.393
Between the dark and the rain,
you can't see shit.

00:44:22.527 --> 00:44:24.095
Just a million umbrellas.

00:44:24.195 --> 00:44:26.331
We'll keep going over it,
in case we missed something.

00:44:26.431 --> 00:44:27.899
The medical examiner confirmed

00:44:27.999 --> 00:44:30.368
that the victim died
of a single gunshot wound.

00:44:30.468 --> 00:44:32.804
The preliminary report
estimated her death

00:44:32.904 --> 00:44:34.072
at approximately 8 p.m.

00:44:34.205 --> 00:44:35.741
Right when the game
got rained out.

00:44:35.841 --> 00:44:37.442
Thousands of fans
rushed to their cars,

00:44:37.542 --> 00:44:40.045
yet we have no witnesses
to the actual shooting.

00:44:40.879 --> 00:44:42.213
[sighs]

00:44:44.382 --> 00:44:45.984
Should we have canceled
the game?

00:44:46.852 --> 00:44:48.453
Statistically?

00:44:49.487 --> 00:44:50.989
No.

00:44:51.089 --> 00:44:52.590
The question I have is:

00:44:52.724 --> 00:44:53.992
Was the victim random

00:44:54.092 --> 00:44:55.592
- or targeted?
- Right.

00:44:55.593 --> 00:44:57.395
And if the Five Borough Killer
is true to his name,

00:44:57.528 --> 00:44:59.898
does this mean the city
should expect four more murders?

00:44:59.998 --> 00:45:02.633
♪ percussive music ♪

00:45:16.547 --> 00:45:18.016
There's coffee in the kitchen.

00:45:18.116 --> 00:45:19.584
Help yourself.

00:45:19.684 --> 00:45:21.887
♪ somber music ♪

00:45:24.622 --> 00:45:26.825
[sighs softly]

00:45:29.961 --> 00:45:31.461
- Excuse me.
- [officer] Yes?

00:45:31.462 --> 00:45:33.098
What floor is Homicide on?

00:45:36.601 --> 00:45:38.703
- Detective Wallace?
- Yes?

00:45:38.804 --> 00:45:39.971
I'm Joey Quinn.

00:45:40.105 --> 00:45:41.606
How can I help you, Mr. Quinn?

00:45:41.706 --> 00:45:43.074
We spoke on the phone
a while back

00:45:43.174 --> 00:45:44.976
about a former colleague
of mine at Miami Metro.

00:45:45.110 --> 00:45:46.344
Angel Batista.

00:45:47.378 --> 00:45:49.247
I recall that conversation.

00:45:49.347 --> 00:45:51.481
Is there somewhere private
we could talk?

00:45:51.482 --> 00:45:53.751
♪ mysterious music ♪

00:45:59.124 --> 00:46:01.159
[sighs]

00:46:19.144 --> 00:46:21.646
[Dexter] <i>Every one of these,
a work of art.</i>

00:46:21.746 --> 00:46:25.083
<i>But I have to keep them all
in the dark.</i>

00:46:29.154 --> 00:46:31.022
Spatter matters, huh, son?

00:46:31.156 --> 00:46:33.324
- [microwave beeping]
- [Dexter sighs]

00:46:34.325 --> 00:46:36.527
[Harry]
What are you looking for?

00:46:36.627 --> 00:46:38.429
You already know he's dead.

00:46:41.399 --> 00:46:43.869
I want to find out
if anyone else knows.

00:46:44.002 --> 00:46:46.838
Since when do you care what
anyone else thinks about you?

00:46:47.738 --> 00:46:48.874
You know, Dex,

00:46:49.007 --> 00:46:50.508
you've been pushing yourself
lately.

00:46:50.608 --> 00:46:51.876
- [sighs]
- Taking risks

00:46:51.877 --> 00:46:53.210
you never used to take.

00:46:53.211 --> 00:46:55.881
Putting yourself
in some serious danger.

00:46:55.981 --> 00:46:58.016
It's like you're trying
to prove something.

00:46:58.116 --> 00:47:01.352
That you're as good as
or better than you've ever been.

00:47:01.452 --> 00:47:03.188
I am.

00:47:03.321 --> 00:47:05.523
♪ tense music ♪

00:47:06.657 --> 00:47:08.059
[Five Borough Killer on video]
<i>Nobody cares.</i>

00:47:08.193 --> 00:47:09.928
<i>- What?</i>
- [silenced gunshot]

00:47:17.468 --> 00:47:19.704
[indistinct chatter]

00:47:43.128 --> 00:47:45.396
[phone chimes]

00:47:52.403 --> 00:47:55.173
[Dexter] <i>I've been killing
killers for half my life.</i>

00:47:55.273 --> 00:47:57.275
<i>More than half my life.</i>

00:47:57.375 --> 00:47:58.775
<i>But no one knows.</i>

00:47:58.776 --> 00:48:00.744
[woman screams]

00:48:00.745 --> 00:48:01.779
Oh, my...

00:48:01.879 --> 00:48:03.081
[breathing heavily]

00:48:03.181 --> 00:48:04.815
[crying]
Oh, my God.

00:48:05.984 --> 00:48:07.552
[Dexter]
<i>So, yeah,</i>

00:48:07.652 --> 00:48:09.354
I want people to notice.

00:48:10.221 --> 00:48:12.590
[Harry] <i>You've taken out
so many bad guys,</i>

00:48:12.723 --> 00:48:14.559
<i>saved countless lives.</i>

00:48:14.659 --> 00:48:16.627
<i>That's a good thing.</i>

00:48:17.828 --> 00:48:19.530
That was always enough for you.

00:48:19.630 --> 00:48:21.599
Maybe now I want more.

00:48:21.699 --> 00:48:23.734
That's the problem
right there, son.

00:48:23.834 --> 00:48:26.004
It's not safe for
a serial killer to want more.

00:48:26.104 --> 00:48:27.973
[sighs]

00:48:28.739 --> 00:48:30.141
I guess I got a problem, then.

00:48:30.241 --> 00:48:32.477
You're unhappy
with where your life is,

00:48:32.610 --> 00:48:35.846
feeling unappreciated,
trying to prove yourself.

00:48:35.947 --> 00:48:38.615
[anchor over TV] <i>We warn viewers
that what you're about to hear</i>

00:48:38.616 --> 00:48:40.151
<i>may be deeply distressing.</i>

00:48:40.285 --> 00:48:41.785
[distorted voice]
<i>Sammy, Sammy, Sammy.</i>

00:48:41.786 --> 00:48:43.653
- [laughing]
<i>- It's your old friend</i>

00:48:43.654 --> 00:48:45.123
<i>the New York Ripper calling...</i>

00:48:45.256 --> 00:48:47.492
[Dexter] <i>What's wrong
with wanting to be appreciated?</i>

00:48:47.625 --> 00:48:49.659
Know what I think this is, Dex?

00:48:49.660 --> 00:48:51.329
You're having a midlife crisis.

00:48:51.462 --> 00:48:55.166
Which is fine if you're a normal
50-something-year-old man.

00:48:55.300 --> 00:48:57.235
Sleep with a younger woman,
buy a red Porsche,

00:48:57.335 --> 00:48:59.137
drive a little too fast.

00:49:00.905 --> 00:49:02.573
But you...

00:49:04.575 --> 00:49:06.644
The stakes are much higher.

00:49:08.179 --> 00:49:10.081
<i>The risks far greater.</i>

00:49:10.181 --> 00:49:12.017
I mean, hell,

00:49:12.117 --> 00:49:13.985
your own son is a damn cop.

00:49:14.119 --> 00:49:16.354
♪ tense music ♪

00:49:18.323 --> 00:49:19.890
[Dexter]
<i>A midlife crisis.</i>

00:49:19.991 --> 00:49:22.326
[sighs heavily]

00:49:22.327 --> 00:49:24.895
<i>For someone who does what I do?</i>

00:49:25.696 --> 00:49:27.832
<i>I'm not ready for that.</i>

00:49:30.135 --> 00:49:31.502
<i>Are you?</i>

00:49:34.505 --> 00:49:36.707
♪ dark music ♪

